.*
.* DSPSAVF: a save file's contents. Save files come in Phase 11; the
.* panel shows the file and an empty list until then.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 40'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=SAVF CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SAVFLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SAVLIB CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJS CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJATR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJSIZE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=OBJS VARS='OPT OBJ OBJTYPE OBJATR OBJSIZE OBJTEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/SFKEYS' NAME=SFKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPSAVF KEYL=SFKEYS HELP=DSPSAVF ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Saved Objects - Save File
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SAVF' VAR=SAVF USAGE=OUTPUT.Save file
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SAVFLIB' VAR=SAVFLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SAVLIB' VAR=SAVLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library saved
:DATAI HELP='FLD/OBJS' VAR=OBJS USAGE=OUTPUT.Objects displayed
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=OBJS.(The save file is empty)
:LISTACT HELP='DSPSAVF/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 5'.5=Display
:LISTCOL HELP='DSPSAVF/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJ' VAR=OBJ USAGE=OUTPUT.Object
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJTYPE' VAR=OBJTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJATR' VAR=OBJATR USAGE=OUTPUT.Attribute
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJSIZE' VAR=OBJSIZE USAGE=OUTPUT.Size
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/OBJTEXT' VAR=OBJTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPSAVF.Display Saved Objects - Help
:P.The objects a save file holds and the library they were saved from.
Save files are not in this release: the list is empty.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SFKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SAVF'.Save file
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SAVFLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SAVLIB'.Library saved
:P.The library saved shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJS'.Objects displayed
:P.The objects displayed shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSAVF/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJ'.Object
:P.The object of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJATR'.Attribute
:P.The attribute of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJSIZE'.Size
:P.The size of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSAVF/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
